        {
          "url": "https://github.com/techrote/cybersand/pull/765#issuecomment-7094871368",
          "body": "**Owner correction — diagnostic priority changed (2026-11-23).** LM Studio was **not running** during the original multi-second Godot freeze. The selected model name was incidental: with no server listening, no HTTP 404 model-validation response could have been returned. Primary repro is **LM Studio provider → configured local endpoint with no listener → Send → immediately close Art**. Compare against no-server Send with the Art window left open and Stop-before-close. This PR's existing hosted checks include only one unreachable-port case (the remaining cases use a running mock HTTP server); its passing suite does **not** rule out the owner-observed absent-server / physical Windows GUI problem. The present test also runs headless and programmatically emits the close signal; it is not a native interactive Windows X-button acceptance test. Keep Draft/HOLD; no change to close/cancel semantics until the corrected condition is measured.",
          "user": {
            "login": "techrote",
            "name": "techrote",
            "email": null,
            "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/261801702?v=4",
            "id": 261801702
          },
          "id": 7094871368,
          "pull_request_review_id": null,
          "in_reply_to_id": null,
          "created_at": "2026-11-23T07:56:50Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-11-23T07:56:50Z",
          "review": null,
          "side": null,
          "line": null,
          "start_line": null,
          "path": null,
          "body_html": "<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Owner correction — diagnostic priority changed (2026-11-23).</strong> LM Studio was <strong>not running</strong> during the original multi-second Godot freeze. The selected model name was incidental: with no server listening, no HTTP 404 model-validation response could have been returned. Primary repro is <strong>LM Studio provider → configured local endpoint with no listener → Send → immediately close Art</strong>. Compare against no-server Send with the Art window left open and Stop-before-close. This PR's existing hosted checks include only one unreachable-port case (the remaining cases use a running mock HTTP server); its passing suite does <strong>not</strong> rule out the owner-observed absent-server / physical Windows GUI problem. The present test also runs headless and programmatically emits the close signal; it is not a native interactive Windows X-button acceptance test. Keep Draft/HOLD; no change to close/cancel semantics until the corrected condition is measured.</p>"
        }
      ],
