          "url": "https://github.com/techrote/cybersand/pull/766#issuecomment-7090874487",
          "body": "## #744 exact-source qualification closeout — hosted Linux/Windows PASS, owner NVIDIA still HOLD\n\n**Current HEAD:** `48970266ae3b1ae47d2278d25ea312328078ddbd`; base accepted main `00cdb02f103265b6dc5224c68283e9a0c8cb449f`.\n\n[Godot 4.7 Art session qualification run 45106738619](https://github.com/techrote/cybersand/actions/runs/45106738619) completed **SUCCESS**, both mandatory Linux and hosted Windows jobs SUCCESS. The original Art session-only/native/traffic/Undo suites executed alongside the new real-loopback regression.\n\nNew `test_art_invalid_local_model_close.gd`: **12/12 passed** on each platform, using a real localhost HTTP POST and a 4-KB HTTP 404 invalid-model response while the Art window is hidden (without any model API calls).\n\n| Result | Linux headless | Windows Server 2022 headless |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| Actual request remains active after Hide | PASS | PASS |\n| Failed response terminates, no automatic retry | PASS | PASS |\n| One response; full redacted error in archive | PASS | PASS |\n| No fictitious usage/assistant records | PASS | PASS |\n| Bounded error + exactly two conversation turns | PASS | PASS |\n| Window remains hidden | PASS | PASS |\n| Maximum observed `process_frame` gap | **7.005 ms** | **8.367 ms** |\n| Request-to-terminal elapsed | **117.656 ms** | **135.543 ms** |\n\n**Historical red runs retained without relabelling:** first run failed in the new fixture because `main.tscn` was not given the ordinary Workbench host script; second failed because the `shared_workbench` launch meta was missing. The published HEAD corrects both fixture omissions and passes real Godot on both platforms. No application-source changes were made for those harness repairs.\n\n**Evidence boundary:** These tests prove the corrected error/hide path under hosted loopback conditions. They do **not** establish causation or reproduce the owner's original multi-second Windows 11/NVIDIA + LM Studio freeze. External LM Studio model-loading CPU/GPU contention and physical-driver effects remain outside this evidence. Keep Draft/HOLD and #744 open for owner physical test; no merge/Ready/auto-merge authority.\n\nSuggested single physical acceptance: source-exact Windows build, invalid LM Studio model with Image off, Send→close X, then compare frame responsiveness, error receipt, reopen, and Stop; confirm that the original lockup no longer reproduces.",
          "user": {
            "login": "techrote",
            "name": "techrote",
            "email": null,
            "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/261801702?v=4",
