          "start_line": null,
          "path": null,
          "body_html": "<h2 dir=\"auto\"><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"6546809532\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/techrote/cybersand/issues/744\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/techrote/cybersand/issues/744/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/techrote/cybersand/issues/744\">#744</a> exact-source qualification closeout — hosted Linux/Windows PASS, owner NVIDIA still HOLD</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Current HEAD:</strong> <code class=\"notranslate\">48970266ae3b1ae47d2278d25ea312328078ddbd</code>; base accepted main <code class=\"notranslate\">00cdb02f103265b6dc5224c68283e9a0c8cb449f</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/techrote/cybersand/actions/runs/45106738619\">Godot 4.7 Art session qualification run 45106738619</a> completed <strong>SUCCESS</strong>, both mandatory Linux and hosted Windows jobs SUCCESS. The original Art session-only/native/traffic/Undo suites executed alongside the new real-loopback regression.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">New <code class=\"notranslate\">test_art_invalid_local_model_close.gd</code>: <strong>12/12 passed</strong> on each platform, using a real localhost HTTP POST and a 4-KB HTTP 404 invalid-model response while the Art window is hidden (without any model API calls).</p>\n<markdown-accessiblity-table><table role=\"table\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Result</th>\n<th align=\"right\">Linux headless</th>\n<th align=\"right\">Windows Server 2022 headless</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Actual request remains active after Hide</td>\n<td align=\"right\">PASS</td>\n<td align=\"right\">PASS</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Failed response terminates, no automatic retry</td>\n<td align=\"right\">PASS</td>\n<td align=\"right\">PASS</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>One response; full redacted error in archive</td>\n<td align=\"right\">PASS</td>\n<td align=\"right\">PASS</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>No fictitious usage/assistant records</td>\n<td align=\"right\">PASS</td>\n<td align=\"right\">PASS</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Bounded error + exactly two conversation turns</td>\n<td align=\"right\">PASS</td>\n<td align=\"right\">PASS</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Window remains hidden</td>\n<td align=\"right\">PASS</td>\n<td align=\"right\">PASS</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Maximum observed <code class=\"notranslate\">process_frame</code> gap</td>\n<td align=\"right\"><strong>7.005 ms</strong></td>\n<td align=\"right\"><strong>8.367 ms</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Request-to-terminal elapsed</td>\n<td align=\"right\"><strong>117.656 ms</strong></td>\n<td align=\"right\"><strong>135.543 ms</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Historical red runs retained without relabelling:</strong> first run failed in the new fixture because <code class=\"notranslate\">main.tscn</code> was not given the ordinary Workbench host script; second failed because the <code class=\"notranslate\">shared_workbench</code> launch meta was missing. The published HEAD corrects both fixture omissions and passes real Godot on both platforms. No application-source changes were made for those harness repairs.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Evidence boundary:</strong> These tests prove the corrected error/hide path under hosted loopback conditions. They do <strong>not</strong> establish causation or reproduce the owner's original multi-second Windows 11/NVIDIA + LM Studio freeze. External LM Studio model-loading CPU/GPU contention and physical-driver effects remain outside this evidence. Keep Draft/HOLD and <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"6546809532\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/techrote/cybersand/issues/744\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/techrote/cybersand/issues/744/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/techrote/cybersand/issues/744\">#744</a> open for owner physical test; no merge/Ready/auto-merge authority.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Suggested single physical acceptance: source-exact Windows build, invalid LM Studio model with Image off, Send→close X, then compare frame responsiveness, error receipt, reopen, and Stop; confirm that the original lockup no longer reproduces.</p>"
